To distinguish between **admission eligibility**, **financial assistance**, and **program-specific conditions** for applying to IIT Jodhpur, here is a structured breakdown based on the retrieved context: --- ### **1. Admission Eligibility** - **Undergraduate Programs**: - Applicants must meet the minimum academic criteria (e.g., 70% marks or 7.0 CPI/CGPA for GEN/GEN-EWS/OBC; 65% for SC/ST/PD) in a qualifying degree (e.g., B.Sc., B.E., B.Pharm, etc.). - Must not be enrolled in any other academic program (full-time or part-time) in India or abroad. - Provisional admissions require submission of mark sheets, provisional certificates, and other documents by the deadline specified in the Academic Calendar. - **Ph.D. Programs**: - Candidates must hold a **minimum four-year bachelor’s degree** in engineering, science, medicine, pharmacy, agricultural science, veterinary science, design, or architecture. - **Regular Ph.D. candidates** cannot be registered in any other academic program or employed full-time/part-time elsewhere. - **SC/ST/PD candidates** are eligible for relaxation in qualifying degree marks as per Ministry of Education rules. --- ### **2. Financial Assistance** - **Eligibility**: - Exceptional regular full-time candidates with a **valid UGC-NET** qualification or a **full-time postgraduate degree of two years or more** from an Institute of National Importance (INI) may be considered for financial assistance. - **Note**: Eligibility does not guarantee financial assistance. - GATE-exempt candidates (as per MHRD guidelines) may also qualify. - **Application**: - Details about fees and financial assistance for PhD programs are available [here](https://www.iitj.ac.in/office-of-academics/en/academic-regulations#top10.6%20Fulfillment%20of%20Admission%20Requirements). --- ### **3. Program-Specific Conditions** - **Ph.D. Programs**: - Full-time Ph.D. students must dedicate all their time to research. Part-time students are working professionals required to attend with limited credits. - Shortlisted candidates must submit the **final application form** (duly signed) and copies of all educational testimonials at the time of admission. - The Senate reserves the right to cancel admissions if documents are not submitted by the deadline or if false information is provided. - **General Rules**: - All admissions (undergraduate or Ph.D.) require **Senate approval**. - Provisional admissions may be canceled if candidates fail to meet document submission deadlines or provide inaccurate information. --- ### **Key Differentiation** - **Admission Eligibility**: Focuses on academic qualifications, enrollment status, and document submission requirements. - **Financial Assistance**: Separate criteria (e.g., UGC-NET, INI degrees) and does not guarantee aid. - **Program-Specific Conditions**: Governs application processes, enrollment rules, and academic conduct (e.g., full-time vs. part-time Ph.D. requirements). For further details, refer to the official guidelines [here](https://www.iitj.ac.in/office-of-academics/en/academic-regulations).

